WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.990
Mendel counted the seeds
from one pea cross:

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.190
7324 in all.

3
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:12.310
5474 were round; 1850 were wrinkled.

4
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:20.520
An exact three to one would give
5493 round seeds and 1831 wrinkled.

5
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.740
Close, but not exact.

6
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.090
Real counts almost never
match a ratio exactly.

7
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.870
So how close is close enough?

8
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.650
In this mission, you'll work
through Mendel's numbers,

9
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.480
comparing what he observed
with what he expected,

10
00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.880
class by class.

11
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.530
Then you'll learn the slips
that catch people out,

12
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.120
from using percentages to
scaling to the wrong total.

13
00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:45.790
Your mission: find out
how close is close enough.
